## Recipe for fullcorn rye sourdough bread

###Ingredients
- 4 tbsp sourdough culture (rye + water)
- 350 g rye flour
- 500 ml water
- 1 kg fullcorn rye flour
- salt
- sunflower seeds, pumpkin seeds, sesam, linseeds after personal taste
- 400 ml water
- some butter

### Procedure
#### Pre-dough
- blend sourdough, 350 grye flour and 500 ml water 
- leave in standing for 24 hours in warm place
- extract 4 tsp of the dough and store in fridge as sourdough starter culture for next time

#### Bread dough
- blend rest of pre-dough with 1 kg rye flour and other dry ingredients
- add 400 ml water (handwarm)
- stir the dough until it is smooth
- use large bread baking form and butter it
- fill dough into bread baking form
- leave it rest for couple of hours until it rises
- bake it for 50-60 min with 200 ˚C 
